  "independence_statement": "Each case is a short story with a hand-chosen frozen workset, an event timeline and hand-written outcomes. The outcomes follow the written blueprint rules: one accepted terminal per frozen occurrence, claim-fenced atomic acceptance, accepted-key reuse on replay, bridge-closed cancel with drain, and a pending workset until the finalizer commits. No msgloom store, finalizer, runner or A2 code was run or imported. The reference checker in the test file only validates the hand-written answers.",
  "provenance": {
    "sources": [
      "A2 Kedro v2 architecture blueprint of 2026-10-23, section 4.2: every ordered frozen occurrence needs exactly one persisted accepted terminal; the deduplicated selection refs are not enough; COMPLETE only when everything is accepted and complete; any limitation gives terminal INCOMPLETE",
      "same blueprint, section 4.3: the versioned finalizer re-checks the PREPARE claim and every accepted result; a failed step rolls back and the workset stays pending; a missing ref or an invalid claim cannot become a success",
      "same blueprint, section 5.1: the logical key is deterministic and includes the frozen configuration version; the key does not include time, attempt or output digest; replay finds the key and returns the stored result; the original record stays unchanged",
      "same blueprint, section 5.3: append_or_verify_a2_stage requires the live claim first, then reuses an accepted key or inserts one atomic record; an accepted prefix written by earlier attempts is reusable; post-COMMIT cancel is not a rollback; the next run skips accepted stages and does not rerun the parser",
      "same blueprint, section 6.1: one owner runner worker per workset; on cancel the bridge-closed flag is set, later nodes and new saves are rejected, then in-flight work drains",
      "same blueprint, section 8.2: outcome table (claim lost gives FAILED scheduled-claim-lost; user cancel gives CANCELLED scheduled-cancelled; trusted partial gives INCOMPLETE scheduled-preparation-incomplete)",
      "A2 Kedro v2 execution plan of 2026-10-23, task T0-07: crash, restart, late writes and cancel; the accepted prefix is saved and unfinished work must be replayable",
      "PROPOSED POLICY (T0-07-P10 only): the blueprint does not say whether an operator replay may run under a changed configuration. See the case rationale.",
      "TASK GOAL (T0-07-P05 only): the task goal says cancel drains pending writes. See the case rationale."
    ]
  },
  "model": {
    "ops": "claim = a process takes the live claim token for a configuration (first run, restart or takeover; it replaces the previous live token); crash = the process dies, uncommitted work is lost; cancel = the bridge-closed flag is set; write = one occurrence result is saved with the named claim token; finalize = the finalizer tries to move the workset from pending to terminal",
    "write_outcomes": "accepted = new atomic accepted record; reused = the key was already accepted, the stored id is returned and the parser does not run; rejected_stale_claim = the token is not the live token, checked before anything else; rejected_bridge_closed = a new save after cancel; rolled_back = the transaction did not reach COMMIT, nothing is stored",
    "finalize_outcomes": "terminal_complete, terminal_incomplete, rejected_stale_claim, rejected_missing_accepted (some frozen occurrence has no accepted result; the workset stays pending)",
    "accepted_prefix": "the frozen occurrences are processed in order by one owner worker, so the accepted set of one configuration is always the first k occurrences",
    "result_ids": "res-<config>-<ordinal> are hand-chosen placeholders for the deterministic accepted result of that configuration and occurrence",
    "snapshot": "state after the named event; accepted lists the accepted occurrence ordinals per configuration; replayable is frozen minus accepted for the active configuration"
  },
